+# TLS Backend Policy
+
+The project's current recorded decision is to use rustls as the TLS backend. It was chosen because it is a pure-Rust TLS implementation with no C dependencies, which avoids the FFI complexity, maintenance burden, and security surface of C bindings. This decision has not been superseded by any later recorded decision.
